From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas571x: TAS5713 (steelhead) — expose the hardware biquad EQ controls

The TAS5713's DAP has the same per-channel speaker-EQ bank as the TAS5707:
7 biquads per channel at the same I2C subaddresses (0x29-0x2f ch1, 0x30-0x36
ch2), each holding five 3.23 fixed-point coefficients (b0,b1,b2,a1,a2; bits
[31:26] of each 32-bit word ignored, unity b0 = 0x00800000). The driver
already has everything needed -- the TAS5707 register defines and the
multiword coefficient accessors -- but tas5713_controls (added for the
steelhead volume-scale fix) exposes only volume/mute, so the EQ bank is
unreachable from userspace.

Add the 14 BIQUAD_COEFS integer-array controls to tas5713_controls, exactly
as the TAS5707 exposes them. Coefficient I/O bypasses regmap (multiword I2C
transfers), so no regmap changes are needed; the PDN GPIO is never toggled
after probe and the DAP keeps register state with MCLK gated, so programmed
coefficients survive sink suspend and are lost only on power loss --
userspace re-applies them at boot (on the Nexus Q: nexusq-control's EQ
support, which drives a bass/treble shelving EQ requested in GitHub
issue #2).

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c
index ceb81b3ad..0c58ce42d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas571x.c
@@ -924,6 +924,30 @@ static const struct snd_kcontrol_new tas5713_controls[] = {
 		   TAS571X_SOFT_MUTE_REG,
 		   TAS571X_SOFT_MUTE_CH1_SHIFT, TAS571X_SOFT_MUTE_CH2_SHIFT,
 		   1, 1),
+
+	/* The TAS5713's DAP carries the same per-channel EQ bank as the
+	 * TAS5707 -- 7 biquads per channel at the same subaddresses
+	 * (0x29-0x2f / 0x30-0x36; five coefficients b0,b1,b2,a1,a2 in 3.23
+	 * format, bits [31:26] ignored) -- so it can reuse the TAS5707
+	 * register defines and the multiword coefficient accessors, which
+	 * bypass regmap. The PDN GPIO is not toggled after probe and the DAP
+	 * keeps register state with MCLK gated, so coefficients survive sink
+	 * suspend; they are lost on power-off, so whoever programs them must
+	 * re-apply at boot (on the Nexus Q: nexusq-control). */
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 0", TAS5707_CH1_BQ0_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 1", TAS5707_CH1_BQ1_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 2", TAS5707_CH1_BQ2_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 3", TAS5707_CH1_BQ3_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 4", TAS5707_CH1_BQ4_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 5", TAS5707_CH1_BQ5_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH1 - Biquad 6", TAS5707_CH1_BQ6_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 0", TAS5707_CH2_BQ0_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 1", TAS5707_CH2_BQ1_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 2", TAS5707_CH2_BQ2_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 3", TAS5707_CH2_BQ3_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 4", TAS5707_CH2_BQ4_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 5", TAS5707_CH2_BQ5_REG),
+	BIQUAD_COEFS("CH2 - Biquad 6", TAS5707_CH2_BQ6_REG),
 };
 
 static const struct tas571x_chip tas5713_chip = {
